.TH EZYVIEW\-MCP 1 "23 October 2026" "EzyView 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezyview\-mcp \- run EzyView's bundled MCP server for AI clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezyview\-mcp
.RI [ client \-supplied \ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezyview\-mcp
runs the Model Context Protocol server that EzyView ships under
.IR /usr/lib/EzyView/mcp/ezyview-mcp.mjs ,
over
.BR stdio .
Register it with an MCP client such as Claude:
.PP
.B claude mcp add ezyview \-\- ezyview\-mcp
.PP
The server exposes workspace and journal snapshots, alerts, indicator and
option pricing data. It is local-only: nothing is sent to a network service.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Node.js 22 or newer on
.BR PATH .
On Mint/Ubuntu the Debian package recommends
.BR nodejs ,
but the distribution's package may be older than 22; install from nodejs.org
or a NodeSource repository when needed. Check with
.B ezyview-mcp \-\-help
after EzyView shows the runtime status in Settings \[->] Desktop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EZYVIEW_MCP_FILE
Run this
.I .mjs
file instead of the bundled one (source checkouts set it to
.IR packages/mcp-server/dist/ezyview-mcp.mjs ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/EzyView/mcp/ezyview-mcp.mjs
The server that is run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/com.printezy247.ezyview/workspace-snapshot.json
Snapshot the desktop app keeps current; the server reads it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ezyview (1)
.PP
The project home page at
.IR https://github.com/printezy247/EzyView .
